## Development

Use [Mise](https://mise.jdx.dev/) to install the tools and run the project's development tasks.

{% if project_type == 'python-api' -%}
Run the API with `uv run {{ project_name }}`. It serves `/health` on port 8000.
{% elif project_type == 'python-api-with-ui' -%}
Run the API with `uv run {{ project_name }}` and the UI with `uv run streamlit run src/{{ project_name | replace('-', '_') }}/ui.py --server.address 0.0.0.0`.
{% endif %}

{% if include_containers %}
## Containers

Build the API image with `docker build -f Dockerfile.api -t {{ project_name }}-api:local .`.
{% if project_type == 'python-api-with-ui' %}
Build the UI image with `docker build -f Dockerfile.ui -t {{ project_name }}-ui:local .`.
{% endif %}
{% if include_compose %}
Run the local services with `docker compose up --build`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if include_kubernetes %}
## Kubernetes

Review the rendered resources with `kubectl kustomize kubernetes/base`. Build and
make the referenced images available to your chosen cluster before applying
these manifests. The template does not create or configure a cluster.
{% endif %}
{% if include_flux %}
## Flux

The `kubernetes/flux` bundle requires an existing Flux controller and
reconciliation root to include these files. It does not install Flux or apply
resources.
{% endif %}
